    "media:imagetext": "TWA\nEMPLOYEES' TIMETABLE\nINTERNATIONAL ADVANCE SCHEDULES\nISSUED DATE JANUARY 31, 1975\nTRANSMITTAL 4-75\nEFFECTIVE APRIL 1, 1975\n(Except as Noted)\nTWA's Peak Summer schedule program includes 170 weekly transatlantic roundtrips, of which 84\nwill be operated with Boeing 747s. These are:\n• Twice daily New York-London\n• Daily Chicago-London\n• Daily San Francisco/Los Angeles-London/Paris\n• Daily Boston-London\n• Daily New York-Paris\n• Daily New York-Frankfurt\n• Daily New York-Lisbon/Madrid\n• Daily New York-Madrid\n• Daily New York-Milan\n• Daily New York-Rome\n• Daily New York-Athens-Tel Aviv\nAdditional improvements in this schedule include:\n• New York-Shannon - increase to twice daily nonstop service.\n• New York-Cairo - increase to daily two-stop service.\n• Madrid-Rome/Athens - increase to daily service.\n• Washington-Paris - reinstatement of daily nonstop service.\n• New York-Switzerland - daily nonstop service to Zurich and Geneva.\n• New York-Paris - increase to twice daily nonstop service.\nThe following additional U.S. cities will receive direct daily service to Europe:\nSan Francisco, Oakland, Las Vegas, Tucson, Phoenix, Denver, Kansas City,\nSt. Louis, Detroit, Cleveland, Pittsburgh, and Philadelphia.\nBUR\nWON\n6\n7\n13\n14\n20\n21\n27\n28\nAPRIL\nTUE\n1\nWED\nTHU\nPRI\nBAT\n2\n3\n10\n11\n12\n16\n17\n18\n19\n22\n23\n24 25 26\n29\n30\nTWA FORM T211 1-75\nSUN\nMOR\nTUE\nMAY\nW7EO\n4\n6\n7\n11\n12\n13\n14\n18\n19\n20\n21\n25\n26 27 28\n9\n15\n16\n22 23\n29 30\n24\n31\n15\n16\n22\n23\n29\n30\nJUNE\nTUE WED\n3\nTHU\nSAT\n4\n5\n6\n7\n10\n11\n17\n12\n13\n14\n18\n19\n20\n21\n24 25\n26 27\n28\nJULY\nSUM\nMON\nTUE\n1\nWED\nTHU\n2\n6\n7\n9\n10\n13\n14\n15\n16\n17\n20\n21\n22\n: 23\n24\n27 28\n29\n30\n31\nFRI\n4\n11\n12\n18\n19\n25 26\nPRINTED IN U.S.A.",
